# Step 5.4 — team activity logs. Run `bun run dev`; VS Code "REST Client" keeps cookies.
@base = http://localhost:3000
@origin = http://localhost:3000
@teamId = REPLACE_WITH_A_TEAM_ID
@hackathon = REPLACE_WITH_A_HACKATHON_SLUG

### Sign in (the team's leader, or an admin)
POST {{base}}/api/auth/sign-in/email
Content-Type: application/json
Origin: {{origin}}

{ "email": "pat@example.com", "password": "REPLACE_ME" }

### Team log — the CURRENT LEADER (live team) or an ADMIN (any team, incl. deleted ones).
### Newest first: { data: { entries: [{ id, action, createdAt, actor: { name },
### target: { name }, details }] }, nextCursor }. Admins also get actorUserId, targetUserId,
### metadata, requestId. Not the leader → 403 NOT_LEADER.
GET {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/audit?limit=20

### …filtered: category = team | requests | invites
GET {{base}}/api/teams/{{teamId}}/audit?category=requests

### ADMIN only: a hackathon's deleted teams (from their TEAM_DELETED rows). Open one with the
### team-log request above, using its teamId.
GET {{base}}/api/admin/hackathons/{{hackathon}}/deleted-teams
